{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123721","id":4605258068,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEn6pVA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123721","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123721.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123721.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123721","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123721/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123721/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123721/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/21fa5b694b0d11f2059940cdd0ca8d759261a5aa","number":123721,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"🤖 macOS: Fix crash when running `--embedded` without a debugger connection","user":{"login":"n3at18","id":30919226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTE5MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30919226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18","html_url":"https://github.com/n3at18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!INFO] *AI disclosure*: This contribution was authored by an autonomous AI agent, on behalf of a user, to fix a crash they hit while using `--embedded` to render a Godot project without an on-screen window.\n\n### Bug\n\nOn macOS, starting the engine with `--embedded` outside the editor crashes immediately, while the display server is still being created:\n\n```\nhandle_crash: Program crashed with signal 11\n```\n\nThe backtrace symbolizes into MoltenVK frames, which makes it look like a rendering or shader-compilation fault. It is not — it is a null dereference.\n\n`DisplayServerMacOSEmbedded` reports back to the editor over the debugger connection (`game_view:set_context_id`, cursor, mouse mode, IME). Those call sites dereference `EngineDebugger::get_singleton()` unconditionally, but the singleton only exists when the process was started by the editor. The first one runs in the constructor, so the crash happens before anything is drawn.\n\n`OS_MacOS_Embedded::alert()` already guards its own message with exactly this check, so the \"no debugger\" case was anticipated on the OS side but missed in the display server.\n\n### Fix\n\nRoute the seven messages through a small helper that drops them when there is no debugger, matching the existing style in `os_macos.mm`. Editor-hosted embedding is unaffected — the singleton is present there and every message is sent as before.\n\n### Result\n\n`--embedded` now runs standalone and renders normally into its off-screen layer, with no window of its own. That makes it usable for scripted runs and screenshot capture on a machine where an extra window would steal focus — close to what [godot-proposals#5790](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5790) asks for, using machinery the engine already has.\n\n### Testing\n\nTested on macOS 26.6.2, Apple M4 Pro, built from `4.7.2-stable` with the same patch.\n\nBefore: crash on startup, as above.\nAfter: the project runs to completion and a screenshot saved from the root viewport shows the scene rendered correctly (Metal, Forward+, ~113 fps).\n\n```\ngodot --embedded --path <project> --script <capture.gd> --resolution 1280x720\n```\n\nWhere `capture.gd` is a `SceneTree` script that instantiates a scene, waits some frames, and calls `root.get_texture().get_image().save_png(...)`.\n\nNo automated test is included: the engine's test suite drives display servers through `DisplayServerMock` on top of `DisplayServerHeadless`, and exercising `DisplayServerMacOSEmbedded` needs a real CoreAnimation/Metal context on macOS, which the headless test runner does not provide. Happy to add one if there is a harness for this that I have missed.\n\n### Notes for reviewers\n\n- The commit is against `master`; it was compiled and run against `4.7.2-stable`, where the code is identical apart from context lines.\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T18:05:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T18:21:17Z","closed_at":"2026-09-22T18:21:11Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c8a17bb56d8c2a0b7c5f07cba54c7811a0f44106","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"n3at18:macos-embedded-no-debugger","ref":"macos-embedded-no-debugger","repo":{"id":1382102900,"node_id":"R_kgDOUmE3dA","name":"godot","full_name":"n3at18/godot","owner":{"login":"n3at18","id":30919226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTE5MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30919226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/n3at18","html_url":"https://github.com/n3at18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/